    "reason": "The geometry generator writes each entity model's bones in the order vanilla's baked model draws them - each part's children in its PartDefinition HashMap's iteration order, depth first, replayed over vanilla's own map calls including the copies a whole-mesh scaling, a replaced part and a retain or clear surgery make - where it wrote addOrReplaceChild order; an exact depth tie goes to the part drawn last, so the tie now falls as vanilla's. entity_geometry.json reorders 151 of its 156 keys with every bone and member unchanged and adds four: the giant's, husk's and wither skeleton's armour shells at their scale, and the warden's bioluminescent layer; entity_models.json points those three wearers' armour and the warden's bioluminescent pass at them, the three armour rows dropping their scale member, which the scaled shells carry. Measured against vanilla: the still sweep's moved rows go 0.4492 to 0.3548 (7 better, 1 worse) - the iron-armoured wither skeleton 0.1675 to 0.1378, husk 0.0573 to 0.0313 and armour stand 0.0217 to 0.0000 - the walk sweep's 0.2543 to 0.2437 with no row worse, the armour sweep's iron piglin 2.4531 to 2.4463; the one row that grows, the zombie villager in iron 0.1112 to 0.1182, is decided by a corner on a snapping midpoint. The skeleton family's 3D renders, the piglin's raw armour render, both dumps' entity listing and the tooling and shipped-table digests move with the order; 12 of the 22 compared artifacts hold.",
